{0 httpkit-http1}

Incremental HTTP/1.1 head and body codecs. The only runtime dependencies are
core values and the pure ipaddr authority parser (with its declared dependencies).

{!Httpkit_http1.feed_head} accepts a slice and reports its consumed prefix.
Continue with the unconsumed suffix when the per-call work budget is reached.
Metadata appears only after the complete head passes syntax, authority and
framing checks. A failed decoder is terminal. HTTP/1.0 is explicitly rejected.

Use {!Httpkit_http1.val-body_decoder} for the resulting framing, and poll again
with empty input after the last data to obtain End. Empty input is not EOF;
EOF has a separate operation. One call produces at most one owned body event.
The caller owns unconsumed pipeline or tunnel bytes.

{!Httpkit_http1.encode_request} and {!Httpkit_http1.encode_response} validate
before returning bytes. {!Httpkit_http1.val-body_encoder} enforces the matching
body length and trailer rules. Once output is committed, an encoder error
requires the caller to abort the exchange, not insert another HTTP response.

Policy: reject duplicate or comma-list Content-Length, CL plus TE, unsupported
transfer-coding chains, obsolete folding, and bare LF. Require exactly one valid
request Host and agreement with absolute/CONNECT authority. Hosts use ASCII DNS
labels or bracketed IPv6; userinfo, escapes and empty labels are rejected.
Trailer fields must be declared and cannot carry framing, routing, authentication,
representation interpretation, or connection-control fields listed by the policy.

These codecs do not associate responses with outstanding exchanges or authorize
upgrade handoff; the engine must check the originating request and ownership.

{!modules:Httpkit_http1}
